<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kong, Côte d'Ivoire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kong is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-coast">Côte d'Ivoire</a> that grew from a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wangara">Dyula</a> trading town into the capital of the Kong Empire in the early 18th century. It was a centre of trade in gold, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kola-nut">kola nuts</a> and cloth and of Islamic learning, with mosques built in the Sudanese earthen style. Samori Touré destroyed the town in 1897, and its Great Mosque is part of a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kong-cote-divoire.jpg" alt="Kong, Côte d'Ivoire" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saindou KANGOUTE · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mosqu%C3%A9e_Samory_Tour%C3%A9.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
